title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf log prune before
catalog: CLI command
target: mf log prune before
summary: Make <target> the new root, deleting all older operations

!! Reference

```
Make <target> the new root, deleting all older operations

Usage: mf log prune before [OPTIONS] [TARGET]

Arguments:
  [TARGET]
          Revision label (most recent on the HEAD ancestry path)

Options:
      --id <ID>
          Target operation by id

      --timestamp <TIMESTAMP>
          Most recent operation whose revision timestamp ≤ T (ISO-8601, or @<unix-ms>)

      --force
          Skip the confirmation prompt

      --silent
          Suppress informational output

  -h, --help
          Print help
```
